INCOHERENT recovery-without-failure .recovery row (line 17): fx-init republished v7 from v5, but v5's last bootlog verdict is 'ok' (fx-init rolls forward only from failed/in-progress)
INCOHERENT bootlog-forged-verdict an ADDED '5 ok 999' line has no '5 in-progress' line earlier in this window — fx-init appends in-progress when it starts a boot (init.zig:4387) and the verdict in that SAME boot (the g_boot_decided latch, init.zig:2619/2631/2726/4398), so no boot the host started is behind this line: it was APPENDED by hand. This is the forge that feeds fx-init's boot decision a verdict no boot produced (bootlog_last, init.zig:737): a forged 'ok' makes the next boot skip the roll-forward and keeps a broken generation CURRENT; a forged 'failed' forces one that should not happen
